	quest.0ADFD0E547DAD509.title: "&f&lObtain A Greater Spirit Of Wind"
	quest.0B284FA1163A8846.quest_desc: [
		"Welcome to all the slime, Thanks for playing my modpack. Here are acouple goodies to get you started."
		""
		"&4&l2 Disclamers"
		""
		"1: In your tensura menu (when you click b), there are some quest integrated there as well, with some worth while rewards."
		""
		"2: This is my first pack so there may be mistakes!! There is a discord server where you can upload suggestions/bug repoorts directly there."
	]
	quest.0B284FA1163A8846.quest_subtitle: "Basics"
	quest.0B284FA1163A8846.title: "&f&lWelcome to All the Slime"
	quest.0B307AA3E970B309.quest_desc: [
		"&0&lActive"
		"[Active - Press] Gift Creation - The user can open a menu and produce any of the Divine Protection Skills as a Sub-Skill for Gift. Only works on the user, no gifting other entities divine protections"
		""
		"[Active - In-Slot / Mode] Divine Protection - The user swaps to the Divine Protection Skill to gain the benefits of the Divine Protection created by Gift Creation."
	]
	quest.0B307AA3E970B309.title: "&f&lGift"
	quest.0B9BC536228E88C5.title: "&2&lTrue Dragon"
	quest.0BAE28AF1AA0ABB7.quest_subtitle: "&1These are the mods that might help you out that arent directly integrated to quest"
	quest.0BAE28AF1AA0ABB7.title: "&f&lUseful Mods"
	quest.0BF47FE510B4A0F4.quest_desc: [
		"&0&lActive"
		"[Active - Hold] - Breeder Reactor: While held down, gives the player MP equal to 2% of their maximum every 5 seconds. Each usage has a 3% chance to add 1 level of Rampage which lasts for 30 seconds, which rises to 7% if the player's MP is past their natural maximum. Duration of Rampage increases by 3 seconds upon hitting an enemy. Rampage can only reach level 10 (20 with Mastery)[Configurable]. With Mastery, becomes a toggle ability instead of hold."
		"---Rampage Effect - +5 Armor, +30 Atk, +0.02 Atk Speed, +0.01 Speed, +0.01 Swim Speed, + 0.1 Knockback Resist per Rampage level"
		""
		"[Acitve - Hold] - Enrage: While held down, gives every mob in a 15x15 radius Rampage effect (+1 level each 10 seconds) for 20 seconds. With Spiritual Attack Resistance, reduced to a 25% chance. Costs 100 MP a second."
	]
	quest.0BF47FE510B4A0F4.quest_subtitle: "&fUsage"
	quest.0BF47FE510B4A0F4.title: "&f&lWrath"
	quest.0CC212F73100AC13.quest_desc: ["Beat Each Lower Tier Boss at Least Once"]
	quest.0CC212F73100AC13.quest_subtitle: "&f&lWas it a perilous journey?"
	quest.0CC212F73100AC13.title: "&7&lBoss Completionist"
	quest.0CCE86249528194A.quest_desc: [
		"&0&lPassive"
		"[Passive, True] Evershining Glory - User does not lose max health to spatial attacks and masters skills faster by 4 points"
		""
		"[Passive, Toggle] Danger Sense"
		""
		"[Passive, Toggle] Hostility Identification - Sense all nearby entities and traps. 10-15 blocks"
		""
		"[Passive, Toggle] Automatic Recovery - Ultraspeed regeneration at 1/2 cost"
		""
		"[Passive, Toggle] Accord - dodge chances are ignored 50%."
	]
	quest.0CCE86249528194A.title: "&f&lGlorious"
	quest.0CD4D7D64630C606.quest_desc: [
		"&0&lPassive"
		"[Passive, True] Heavenly Restriction:"
		"The user of this skill can no longer gain any magicules, nor gain any more skills (except for the ones provided to them on reincarnation by their race, OR if a skill was gifted to them, i.e. Hidden Ruler.) They can, however, still gain Battlewills."
		""
		"The user also gains 3 times more Aura than a normal player, to compensate for their lack of Magicules."
		""
		"Since the user has little to no magicules, they cannot be picked up by any magicule sensing skills. They can, however, be picked up by auditory sense or heat sense."
		""
		"[Passive, In Slot] Fearless:"
		"The user cannot be affected by Fear, Slowness or Burden. They also cannot feel any effects of Haki."
		""
		"[Passive, Toggle] Learned Techniques:"
		"The user’s Battlewills do five times more damage than usual. This stacks with [Divine Ki Release] or [Martial Master], if the user should SOMEHOW come into their possession. Additionally, all of the user’s PHYSICAL attacks deal 3x more damage."
		""
		"[Passive, True] Through the Odds (Requires Mastery): On mastery of [Restricted], become able to pierce through all resistances and degrade them."
		""
		"&0&lActive"
		"[Active, Press] Decimate:"
		"Instantly dash 12 blocks ahead (16 blocks on mastery) and deal 20 + a weapon’s critical worth of damage."
		""
		"On mastery, instead deal 1.5 * (35 + Critical Hit damage). This attack can now damage spiritual beings and will bypass Resistances. Costs 500 Aura to use."
		""
		"[Active, Press] Counter:"
		"Consume 1500 aura instantly. Enter a parrying stance for 3 seconds (5 on mastery), accompanied by a loud sound to let opponents have time to react (no sound atm, sound guy was busy)."
		""
		"Movement and Attack Speed are set to zero while this stance is active. Press again while active to cancel, and no cooldown will occur."
		""
		"The next physical attack that hits you will deal zero damage and disables your enemy’s attack speed for 5 seconds as they scramble to recover. If you are successful in a parry, go on a 15 second cooldown"
	]
	quest.0CD4D7D64630C606.title: "&f&lRestricted"
	quest.0CFF6C9BCCD9DF37.quest_desc: [
		"&0&lActive"
		""
		"[Active - Hold] Corrosion: Give user’s physical attack with a corrosion effect when this mode is in Slot. When activated while looking at nothing, costs 200 MP and deals 5 corrosion damage every 10 ticks to all enemies in a 10x10 radius. Enemies killed by this have their Intrinsic, Common, Extra, and Resist Skills taken by the player as well as have 50% of their ep added to the player's maximum. The other 50% is added to Stomach's energy storage. (25 to MP, 25 to AP) - (EP absorb only applies for the first target of that type using Starved)"
		""
		"[Active - Press] Stomach: When activated, grants access to a spatial storage with the size of a chest with 6 rows. Items are able to be stacked to 128 instead of 64."
		""
		"[Active - Press] Receive: When activated while looking at a subordinate, Intrinsic, Common, Extra, and Resist skills owned by it are given to the player."
		""
		"[Active - Press] Spiritual Domination: Like Thought Communication + 1 additional command: Rampage. Activating Rampage command will give 5 minutes of Rampage effect to every subordinate in 30 block radius, activating again or using other commands will remove the effect."
	]
	quest.0CFF6C9BCCD9DF37.quest_subtitle: "&fUsage"
	quest.0CFF6C9BCCD9DF37.title: "&f&lStarved"
	quest.0E1B1415794428AD.quest_desc: [
		"&f&lAfter finding the Adventurer Guild structure, meet Yuuki Kagurazaka, and then formally enter the guild commission system."
		""
		"&6&lGuild Systems"
		"After joining the guild, players receive a member number, signature record, guild profile, and adventurer rank."
		""
		"Commission System: Includes gathering, crafting, subjugation, coordinate-based subjugation, party commissions, and more."
		""
		"Adventurer Ranks: Gain adventurer experience by completing guild commissions and rise from Rank F to Rank S."
		""
		"Dwarf Commissions: Dwarf NPCs issue commissions related to workshops, ores, leather, equipment, butcher materials, and more."
		""
		"Party System: Create or join parties, use party chat, and take on multiplayer commissions."
		""
		"Yuuki Kagurazaka: Adds the Yuuki NPC and Boss fight"
	]
	quest.0E1B1415794428AD.quest_subtitle: "&fInfo"
	quest.0E1B1415794428AD.title: "&f&lJoin A Guild"
	quest.0FC6548B9243C32D.title: "Gain EP (1k)"
	quest.10534FD5FB950E89.quest_desc: [
		"1. Old Eye - Found in Desert Pyramids"
		""
		"Legends say this eye once belonged to one of the great Sandworms"
		""
		"2. Nether Eye - Found in Nether Fortresses"
		""
		"It was lost by a demon in the battle between the Aether and the Nether"
		""
		"3. Cold Eye - Found in Igloos"
		""
		"One of the last artifacts left behind by the Iceologers before they all suddenly vanished from the world"
		""
		"4. Rogue Eye - Found in Jungle Pyramids"
		""
		"This eye is believed to have given our ancestors the knowledge of Redstone"
		""
		"5. Black Eye - Found in Buried Chests"
		""
		"Pirates say it gave sight to the legendary Black Pearl"
		""
		"6. Magical Eye - Dropped by Evokers"
		""
		"Without this eye, the Evoker has no power"
		""
		"7. Lost Eye - Found in Mineshafts"
		""
		"It is told that it was forged by the first blacksmiths of time"
		""
		"8. Corrupted Eye - Found in Pillager Outposts"
		""
		"The eye of a greedy king faded in solitude. Legend says it will bring infinite fortune to its owner"
		""
		"9. Wither Eye - Dropped by The Wither"
		""
		"Has witnessed destruction. Maybe it also witnessed your stuff disappear"
		""
		"10. Guardian Eye - Get it by Killing Elder Guardian"
		""
		"It has seen many warriors drown into the depths of the sea"
		""
		"11. Witch Eye - Craft it using the witch pupil"
		""
		" This pupil is believed to have seen the ancient brewing recipes that were lost in time."
		""
		"12. Cursed Eye - Found in Bastions treasure chest"
		""
		" A powerful yet destructive artifact; the Piglins swore to protect it at the cost of their lives"
		""
		"13. Exotic Eye - Craft it using aquatic items"
		""
		" Those who followed this eye were never seen again; rumors say they found the great city of Atlantis, or lost their way trying"
		""
		"14. Evil Eye - Buy it from a master cleric"
		""
		" A holy talisman said to protect its owner from bad luck"
		""
		"15. Undead Eye - Craft it using an Undead Soul"
		""
		" Remembrance of the past lives of those who live in death"
		""
		"16. Cryptic Eye - Have a small chance to get it when enchanting"
	]
	quest.10534FD5FB950E89.quest_subtitle: "&1&lThat ender eye won't be enough"
	quest.10534FD5FB950E89.title: "&f&lGetting to the end might not be as easy as you thought"
	quest.105B93DE7E9AD78A.quest_desc: [
		"&0&lPassive"
		"[Passive, In Slot] Isha’s Tears - All players, even the wielder, and mobs, regardless of EP, are slowed by the player’s baneful aura. Slowness 4 for 10 seconds while near the player. The wielder only gets Slowness 2. Player gains Resistance 2 passively."
		""
		"[Passive, Toggle] Homing - All thrown objects home in on targets."
		""
		"[Passive, True] Veil - When dropping below 25% HP, knock all entities within a 12 block radius backwards by a large amount and grant them Slowness 10 and Burden 4 for 30 seconds. Cooldown of 5 minutes."
		""
		"&0&lActive"
		"[Active, Press (100.0 MP)] Gust - Generate strong blasts of wind to throw and manipulate objects or deadly, sharpened wind. No cooldown."
		""
		"[Active, Hold] Turbulent Force - Pick up and control the movements of an entity you pick up. Maximum height of 5 blocks. (10 on mastery)."
		""
		"[Active, Press (1000.0 MP.)] Grief - Cry out, knocking back entities within 8 blocks with moderate knock back and inflicting them with blindness and weakness 2 for 10 seconds. Cooldown of 10 seconds"
	]
	quest.105B93DE7E9AD78A.title: "&f&lMelancholy"
	quest.11051710EACFEB48.quest_desc: [
		"&0&lPassive"
		"[ Passive - In Slot ] - Copy: The user can copy an ability's specific mode after being hit or affected by it when [Pride]'s Copy Mode is in slot. Without mastery, it will only be able to copy attacks, such as Absolute Severance. Once mastered, [Pride] will be able to copy abilities when inflicted with status effects like Infinity Prison's Imprison or Healer's Infection. Note that [Pride] won't be able to copy any spirit related magic"
		""
		"---[Pride]'s Mastery gain is based on the copied ability's cost, (Example: you get 1 point per 2500 MP cost, so if the ability costs 10K to acquire, you get 4 mastery points) while cooldown is 5s. On a failed copy, [Pride] will only gain 10% of the mastery it would've gained on a successful copying of the ability, but the cooldown is similarly reduced to 10%."
		""
		"---Once a mode is successfully copied, the user will pay the whole ability's obtainment cost and [Pride] will go on cooldown. The copied mode will be added as a new Mode for [Pride] (If this mode requires learning, it will be instantly learnt once acquired). As this is a new mode on [Pride] itself, the copied skill's passive features won't be usable and a mode may be unusable if it depends on said passive features or other modes of the ability."
		""
		"&0&lActive"
		"[ Active - Press ] - Copy : Opens a new GUI that allows the user to quickly equip or remove copied ability modes."
	]
	quest.11051710EACFEB48.quest_subtitle: "&fUsage"
	quest.11051710EACFEB48.title: "&f&lPride"
	quest.12690AFB6B1F1A93.quest_desc: ["&6&l5% drop &f&lfrom Valentine"]
	quest.133798F44DEF3C39.quest_desc: [
		"&0&lPassive"
		"[Passive, True] Hoe Mastery - All hoes deal increased damage, allowing even a wooden hoe to be useful."
		""
		"[Passive, Toggled] Crop Mastery - Nearby crops have a 50% chance (per crop) every 5 seconds to grow by one stage. allowing you to vastly speed up the process of growing any crops. Consumes 20 MP every 5 seconds when toggled on."
		""
		"&0&lActive"
		"[Active, Press] Blessing - Bless the food stack you're holding. Based on the current time of day, blessing the food will grant various helpful buffs. You can give these foods to any entity as well, allowing you to give buffs to them."
		"For each item in the stack, consume 250 MP. On mastery, the cost increases to 500 MP per food item."
		""
		"Blessed at Dawn: Gain Strengthen 3 for 3 minutes (Strengthen 5 for 5 minutes on mastery) from consuming it. Blessed at Noon: Gain Resistance 1 for 3 minutes (Resistance 2 for 3 minutes on mastery) from consuming it. Blessed at Night: Gain Speed 3 and 2.0 Step Height for 3 minutes (Speed 5 and 3.0 Step Height for 5 minutes on mastery) from consuming it."
		""
		"This mode gains mastery differently! It DIVIDES the points you would gain by 10, based on how many items were in the item stack, rounded down to the nearest whole number. For example, if I had a stack of 64 Steak, I would gain 6 mastery points instead of 1. However, if I were to just bless one, two, three, four, five, eight, or nine items, it would be 0 mastery points. You MUST minimally bless a stack of 10 to gain mastery."
	]
	quest.133798F44DEF3C39.title: "&f&lGardener"
	quest.13C699DA02E67161.quest_desc: ["You need 100k EP"]
	quest.13C699DA02E67161.quest_subtitle: "What are you, A smart guy?!"
	quest.13C699DA02E67161.title: "Enlighntened Human"
	quest.158D1AEE4A149780.quest_subtitle: "Found in Ocean Monuments"
	quest.158D1AEE4A149780.title: "Old Ahh Fish"
	quest.15EC0EB3EF2D8B03.quest_desc: ["Imbues the caster with a buff that automatically dodges the next few incoming attacks by teleporting them away. It completely negates hard-hitting single-target boss strikes."]
	quest.15EC0EB3EF2D8B03.title: "&f&lEvasion"
	quest.16037AE26219E80F.quest_desc: [
		"&0&lPassive"
		"[Passive, toggle] Post-Mortem Surge - The user gains a stacking buff to Attack and Speed for every entity they \"delete.\" This makes the user progressively more dangerous as a battle continues."
		""
		"[Passive, In slot] Atomic Annihilation - Attacks deal 50% more damage and reduces physical resistance. Physical attacks deal Spiritual Damage by vibrating the target's magicules until their internal structure \"evaporates.\" Highly effective against equipment."
		""
		"[Passive, Toggle] Destructive Resonance - Allows the user to coat their body in a \"Dissolution Aura.\" Physical projectiles and low-level magic are disintegrated before they touch the user."
		""
		"&0&lActive"
		"[Active] Tyrant’s Haki - It exerts a heavy gravity-like pressure that drains the stamina of everyone in the vicinity. Those with weak wills are inflicted with the [Fear] and [Despair] status."
		""
		"[Active] End of Days - Targets with EP lower than 75% of the user’s must pass a Soul Resistance check. Failure results in immediate Soul Collapse. (Resistance/Nullification reduces the success rate, but the attempt still deals spiritual damage)."
	]
	quest.16037AE26219E80F.title: "&f&lDevastator"
	quest.1613D749F973F3F1.quest_desc: [
		"&0&lActive"
		"[Active - Press] Divine Release: Grants an effect equivalent to Strength 20, gives the user an additional 20 Armour Points, and +0.06 Speed. It lasts for 3 Minutes and upon ending inflicts the player with Paralysis 2, Fragility 2, and Weakness 2 for 10 Minutes. Mastery increases the duration to 6 Minutes and double the stat boost. During the duration, all damage taken is treated as physical damage. Every battlewill attack the user does in this mode will deal x6 damage (x8 with Mastery). Costs 10,000 MP and deals 10HP in damage every second while active. [Activate again to turn off the effect but still gets the debuff and cooldown]"
	]
	quest.1613D749F973F3F1.quest_subtitle: "&fUsage"
	quest.1613D749F973F3F1.title: "&f&lDivine Berserker"
	quest.16531497164F36C5.quest_subtitle: "To the Nether"
	quest.16531497164F36C5.title: "Gather These!"
	quest.1680DDEEC0E76EF5.quest_desc: [
		"&0&lPassive"
		"[Passive - Toggle] - Makes learning Battlewills and Magic happen instantly"
		""
		"[Passive - True] - The player earns 3x more mastery points with each usage."
		""
		"[Passive - In Slot] - The player gets +75 base damage (+150 With Mastery) Can select damage output by holding skill activation and scrolling mouse wheel."
	]
	quest.1680DDEEC0E76EF5.quest_subtitle: "&fUsage"
	quest.1680DDEEC0E76EF5.title: "&f&lFighter"
